nnessee is his only orange and currently mortgaged. I could propose Tennessee plus $200, which seems reasonable given Claude\u2019s cash of $941. I wonder if he\u2019d accept that offer.**Considering trade proposals**\n\nProposing a high cash deal has no downside and could lead to significant outcomes if accepted. My question is which option we should prioritize. We can make multiple proposals if our first ones are rejected. However, if accepted, we might lose Indiana and reshape our approach, which might not be ideal. The safer option seems to be trading the jail card. I think I'll go for Claude GOOJF for $75.","format":"openai-responses-v1","index":0},{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"gAAAAABqJhnE3D73Q4CjjqjkWoFx_QK0xazlwCFpQQoQmpahmFCbErLxzB7lWFOOfaMfhLaySEH3olmQKg9UAlIm-aZkzKIQsONzx1zint5vlVwHMij7hXUhQER5SLIRkusDrx6pVN4bjrtIYZWbkZkxH9yawzMgfM7W9EC3jAL23F3SJzXDkOtq0C6A7waz0iuan7nVSuxhpDerdAUPoUdKgyDyWyHWvrIVs4eFUBMfb3UddyvnFxDRbeAkUBqg91ZzSj1fQPX9h1L_XRZ3l6JBUbTN4WrmJUaS2_lE2c-1i40zrw1uZ0ECF4UaWgiXbIEwJtqR_XjU-BGh4YelemW4tPjB1MgecoWtZj0_W4Qm7RT7qOURFkAGNhrRZPHzKEjGBNVnGn25e_lk5JoQ9yyWCsTeOjoFcwARWXtDxv9VmLcpa4xN01fxZMIHfuEC9q-vy-j5_qchYwWs5Kc0w3VF40xETA6sZnU-Fxmv1yaVcvNMBYF7Epo5kHdi_6a3Ix55tUO2d0eMSYT7K4EyzU0BiSLfA2bCinR_q_BymSySOLjgP5Xlu7Pvs5rhwkcCoDV-yRmUIeHVY8bsGrnjPTvPPzDfC6vHAESt-vnjD5UAR0uMC23jQHEZ_CD7ZtLkX3qYwcfNzb5j9KBeQO_m6tFwBx8uCN0iiJA8kwonYTqAJHILYDOkZHufzmkQdYIOf1k-H_6pnEe9G6_6560p7_0zXhG_WXNqMqSfUr0sQt12-s-4dPYvGu2bI3Py96dlaoNboyzvQxfv_5hcAY-G0R1Dcqmam2h0gbPLHS_gnQHKaJhA7ojg8VGRItnVaH_C-moJ8s7jbddO9SBFIZMMnLthCrUjMlnspQHmaFelsfkiwOshzsvxvfe3aexIbtsA-URSTDicB2B0q4qn5iji-gkYa9xDxv2LzHcqIY7WIa_Ssf--MYNGTd1mvGjnof6N3PqX_IqZpBd0Ng1hqjYZjo3PHeFvxLaTJCjQ3-eDJVUf8Hu8bxXI5FksESOAu2H6a7E8iqCtALaWFLdAALCyugkEV1XkKdjEnLaNGaoPJXicatvyLXhtlXeQ3zGJBqBdKWwKv50laneidbzDUsqoIrJrA_Sr1rjoPvX961gNEjW-l2B2tXwMMlWRORtk7r1EMC9iW-hMRsVIYq4a9eGsyq9St_e_lzoqaZVQIxkCyD8SlURQt0p9GTtVVK3z-UAcqJVp2S1hZ3myD5ehGw5ZnAmkj84EsuYsNY8i36nLsQHHsmYuA5LSdDu_o-FLRrR3N1Nojg9akDqOe8BrZYeL